@startuml
' Activity 5: edit, review, publish and recall content. Transcribed from Diagram/ACTIVITY/act-5-content.drawio.
' The drawio has ONE merge that both back-edges enter; PlantUML allows one back-edge per loop,
' so it is drawn as two nested repeat loops (two merge diamonds back to back, same meaning).
skinparam wrapWidth 150
|Editor|
|System (BE)|
|Reviewer|
|Manager|

|Editor|
start
repeat
  repeat
    :Save the chapter draft;
    :Submit for review with a change type;
    |System (BE)|
    :Check every path reaches an ending;
  repeat while () is ([a path has no ending]) not ([plays to an ending])
  |Reviewer|
  :Review someone else's draft;
repeat while () is ([return with a reason]) not ([approve])
|Manager|
:Publish a release;
|System (BE)|
if () then ([publisher wrote a draft])
  :Refuse the publish;
  stop
else ([else])
  :Freeze approved drafts, set the version number;
  :Make the new release current;
endif
|Manager|
:Watch the release in play;
if () then ([no defect])
  stop
else ([defect found])
  :Recall the release with a reason;
  |System (BE)|
  :Make the newest older release current;
  stop
endif
@enduml
